<section class="sec" id="overview">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="rv"><p class="plate">Overview</p><h2 class="h2 mt-s">How this division works.</h2>
      <div class="mt-m"><p class="body-copy">Nigeria's energy transition is being driven by economics as much as policy. Compressed natural gas is cheaper per kilometre than petrol and cleaner than diesel, and the constraint has never been demand — it has been infrastructure and conversion capacity.</p><p class="body-copy">We work on both sides of that constraint: building and operating refuelling capacity, and running certified conversion programmes for commercial fleets. For industrial customers we supply gas directly against process and power requirements, structured on term contracts that make budgeting predictable.</p></div></div>
    <div class="rv rv-d1"><p class="plate">Specification</p><div class="spec"><div class="spec__r"><div class="spec__k">Infrastructure</div><div class="spec__v">Refuelling station development, compression and dispensing systems</div></div><div class="spec__r"><div class="spec__k">Supply</div><div class="spec__v">Industrial process gas, power generation feedstock, transport fuel</div></div><div class="spec__r"><div class="spec__k">Conversion</div><div class="spec__v">Certified petrol and diesel vehicle conversion, fleet programmes</div></div><div class="spec__r"><div class="spec__k">Contracting</div><div class="spec__v">Term supply agreements with indexed pricing</div></div><div class="spec__r"><div class="spec__k">Compliance</div><div class="spec__v">Full alignment with national gas policy and safety regulation</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

