<section class="sec tint" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:900px">
    <div class="sec-head rv"><p class="plate">Questions</p><h2 class="h2 mt-s">Answered plainly.</h2></div>
    <div class="acc"><div class="acc__i"><button class="acc__b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cng-0"><span>How much does converting a vehicle save?</span><span class="acc__ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="acc__p" id="cng-0"><div>Savings depend on mileage, engine and current fuel price, so we model each fleet rather than quote a headline figure. High-mileage commercial vehicles reach payback fastest, which is why fleet programmes come first.</div></div></div><div class="acc__i"><button class="acc__b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cng-1"><span>Is a converted vehicle still able to run on petrol?</span><span class="acc__ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="acc__p" id="cng-1"><div>Bi-fuel conversions retain the original fuel system and switch between the two. Dedicated conversions do not, and are only recommended where refuelling access is assured.</div></div></div><div class="acc__i"><button class="acc__b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cng-2"><span>Does conversion affect the vehicle warranty?</span><span class="acc__ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="acc__p" id="cng-2"><div>We use certified kits and certified installers, and we document the installation. Warranty position varies by manufacturer, and we set that out clearly before work starts.</div></div></div><div class="acc__i"><button class="acc__b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cng-3"><span>Can you supply gas to a site with no station nearby?</span><span class="acc__ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="acc__p" id="cng-3"><div>Yes. Industrial customers are served under term supply arrangements rather than forecourt dispensing, sized against your demand profile.</div></div></div><div class="acc__i"><button class="acc__b" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cng-4"><span>Is CNG safe?</span><span class="acc__ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="acc__p" id="cng-4"><div>Handled to standard, yes — cylinders are rated well above operating pressure and gas disperses upward rather than pooling. Safety depends on certified installation and periodic inspection, both of which we hold to.</div></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

